y":0.0288}}],"quotes":[{"c":"PI 2018 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2018-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Brodersen","x":"Total first-quarter operating expense, excluding the impact of the restructuring, was $19.5 million, compared with $19.3 million in the prior quarter.Research and development expense was $6.9 million, sales and marketing were $8 million, and general and administrative expense was $4.6 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/08/impinj-pi-q1-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2018-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Brodersen","x":"We ended the quarter with 284 employees, consistent with our restructuring plan.Our adjusted EBITDA was a loss of $7.1 million, compared with an adjusted EBITDA loss of $5.8 million in the prior quarter and in line with our guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/08/impinj-pi-q1-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2018-09-13","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"Turning briefly to tariffs, the U.S. imposition in late August of a new round of tariffs products manufactured in China affects one pre-Monza R6 endpoint IC wafer product and only those wafers that our inlay partners import and assemble in the U.S. We shipped enough additional inventory to the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/09/14/impinj-pi-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2018-09-13","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"Chris, are you asking a tariff-related question?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/09/14/impinj-pi-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2018-09-13","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Mike Walkley","x":"And last question for me and I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/09/14/impinj-pi-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2018-09-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Brodersen","x":"And as of June 30, 2018, our first-quarter restructuring plan is substantially complete, as we executed a sublease for our vacant office space.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/09/14/impinj-pi-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2018-09-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jeff Dossett","x":"The other impact that we've referred to in previous calls is the restructuring that we undertook in the Asia-Pacific region, which is well under way.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/09/14/impinj-pi-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2018 Q3","e":"pi","d":"2018-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Mike Walkley","x":"Last question from me and I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/29/impinj-inc-pi-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2019 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2019-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Brodersen","x":"The primary driver of the year-over-year decline was lower sales and marketing expense from reduced headcount.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/29/impinj-inc-pi-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2019 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2019-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Brodersen","x":"But as you noted, we're up against a relatively easy compare, when you look back at Q1 of '18 when we had our restructuring and some reader IC constraints.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/29/impinj-inc-pi-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2020 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2020-04-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"Our team is well aware that hospitals and healthcare facilities across the world are using our products in the fight against Covid-19, to track equipment and consumables and to streamline hospital operations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/28/impinj-inc-pi-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2020 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2020-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"We are today seeing traction not only reading items passing through dock doors, which we have discussed on prior calls, but also on conveyor belts, to reduce manual touch and improve shipment accuracy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/impinj-inc-pi-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PI 2024 Q4","e":"pi","d":"2025-02-05","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"Geopolitical uncertainty in tariffs; end users changing label-partner share allocations; aggressive label price shopping; and shorter ordering cycles disrupted partner bookings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/impinj-pi-q4-2024-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2024 Q4","e":"pi","d":"2025-02-05","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"So, our focus is helping our inlay partners clear a few weeks of inventory and together, navigating the geopolitical and tariff landscape.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/impinj-pi-q4-2024-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2025 Q3","e":"pi","d":"2025-10-29","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"We delivered that revenue outperformance despite weak retailer buying patterns and tariff headwinds, highlighting our strong market position, technical and product leadership.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/30/impinj-pi-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2025 Q4","e":"pi","d":"2026-02-05","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"Tariffs, and tariff-related supply chain whipsaws, inventory reductions at every layer of our retail markets, a downward trend in apparel imports, and protracted general merchandise adoption all weighed heavily on the RAIN market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/05/impinj-pi-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2026 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2026-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"We see retail rebuys, especially helped by the tariff clarity and essentially the tariff whipsaws are gone and there's more certainty in the markets associated with tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/impinj-pi-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2026 Q1","e":"pi","d":"2026-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"Part of that reason, of course, was due to retailer destocking and the impact of tariffs and other whipsaws that happened in the market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/impinj-pi-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2026 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2026-07-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Cary Baker","x":"We also saw some pull-ins from the retailers ahead of the tariff -- the July tariff reset.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/impinj-pi-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2026 Q2","e":"pi","d":"2026-07-29","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Diorio","x":"We believe market expansion, retailer pull-ins before temporary tariffs expired last week, and consumer resilience drove the demand strength.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/impinj-pi-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PI 2026 Q3","e":"pi","d":"2026-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Cary Baker","x":"We highlighted how the pricing and the mix environment might be different this year than the last 2 Q1s because our costs are going up, and when we're unable to engineer around those cost increases, we look to pass them on to protect our margin model.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/im